 very  simple some cases that where I have a  translation I listen I save words and  phrases I get to use to it I listen to  the when i first started 20 30 40 times  the point is it's all fun so the message  with web point 20 is we want to get a  lot of interaction we want the learners  to say what they want there may be  learners who want the detailed grammar  explanations personally I recommend  trying to avoid it until you have heard  a lot of the language enjoy stories in  the language and of course what we're  doing at link is we have our learners  giving us content in their own languages  talking about their daily experiences in  their own languages transcribing it  people are trying to learn that language  can download it and listen to it over  and over again maybe create something  back in their own language all of this  is fun language learning is fun language  learning need not be the tedious grammar  based exercise drill based you know you  got it wrong type of thing that we're  used to at school we have to take  language learning away from the school's  away from the textbooks away from the  teachers and give it back to the  learners and that's my message for today
 

